            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A method (400) of operating an optical system (200), the method (400) comprising: receiving (408) data from an eye tracker (240) of the optical system (200), wherein the optical system (200) includes a frame configured to be worn about a head of a user of the optical system (200) and a dimming component (203) carried by the frame and configured to be positioned between an eye of the user and an environment of the user; determining (408), based on the data received from the eye tracker (240), a location within the eye of the user at which a center of rotation of the eye of the user is positioned; identifying one or more points (1802) in three-dimensional space located within the environment of the user; and for each of the one or more identified points (1802) within the environment of the user: identifying (412) a set of one or more pixels (1808) of the dimming component (203) based at least in part on the determined location of the center of rotation of the eye of the user and the respective point in three-dimensional space located within the environment of the user; and controlling (416) the dimming component (203) to dim the identified set of one or more pixels (1808).(Fig. 18B)</p>
            </abstract>
